IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`
IMPORT `sg-groups`
IMPORT `sg-interests`
IMPORT `sgb2-s164-register-of-shareholdings`

-- Tests for s 164. Every expected value is written from the text, beside the assertion, before it was run.

§ `Facts for the s 7 interest tests`

`s 164 test facts: no interest at all` MEANS `s 7 interest facts` WITH
    `the person has authority (formal or informal, express or implied) to dispose of, or to exercise control over the disposal of, the shares` IS FALSE
    `property held in trust consists of or includes the shares and the person has an interest under the trust` IS FALSE
    `the person knows, or has reasonable grounds for believing, that the person has that interest under the trust` IS FALSE
    `the person has entered into a contract to purchase a share` IS FALSE
    `the person has a right, otherwise than by reason of having an interest under a trust, to have a share transferred to the person or to the person's order` IS FALSE
    `the person has the right to acquire a share, or an interest in a share, under an option` IS FALSE
    `the person is entitled, otherwise than as a proxy or representative at a meeting, to exercise or control the exercise of a right attached to a share of which the person is not the registered holder` IS FALSE
    `the thing is a unit in a collective investment scheme that has been subscribed or purchased on an offer of units, or is issued for such an offer and held by the scheme's manager` IS FALSE
    `the person holds the share as bare trustee` IS FALSE
    `the person's ordinary business includes the lending of money` IS FALSE
    `the person holds the interest only by way of security for a transaction entered into in the ordinary course of business in connection with the lending of money` IS FALSE
    `the person holds the interest by reason of holding a prescribed office` IS FALSE
    `the interest is a company's interest in its own shares purchased or otherwise acquired in accordance with sections 76B to 76G (including treasury shares)` IS FALSE
    `the interest is a prescribed interest of a prescribed person or class of persons` IS FALSE
    `the bodies corporate through which the person may be deemed to have the interest` IS EMPTY

`s 164 test facts: a contract to purchase a share` MEANS `s 7 interest facts` WITH
    `the person has authority (formal or informal, express or implied) to dispose of, or to exercise control over the disposal of, the shares` IS FALSE
    `property held in trust consists of or includes the shares and the person has an interest under the trust` IS FALSE
    `the person knows, or has reasonable grounds for believing, that the person has that interest under the trust` IS FALSE
    `the person has entered into a contract to purchase a share` IS TRUE
    `the person has a right, otherwise than by reason of having an interest under a trust, to have a share transferred to the person or to the person's order` IS FALSE
    `the person has the right to acquire a share, or an interest in a share, under an option` IS FALSE
    `the person is entitled, otherwise than as a proxy or representative at a meeting, to exercise or control the exercise of a right attached to a share of which the person is not the registered holder` IS FALSE
    `the thing is a unit in a collective investment scheme that has been subscribed or purchased on an offer of units, or is issued for such an offer and held by the scheme's manager` IS FALSE
    `the person holds the share as bare trustee` IS FALSE
    `the person's ordinary business includes the lending of money` IS FALSE
    `the person holds the interest only by way of security for a transaction entered into in the ordinary course of business in connection with the lending of money` IS FALSE
    `the person holds the interest by reason of holding a prescribed office` IS FALSE
    `the interest is a company's interest in its own shares purchased or otherwise acquired in accordance with sections 76B to 76G (including treasury shares)` IS FALSE
    `the interest is a prescribed interest of a prescribed person or class of persons` IS FALSE
    `the bodies corporate through which the person may be deemed to have the interest` IS EMPTY

`s 164 test facts: a unit and a contract to purchase` MEANS `s 7 interest facts` WITH
    `the person has authority (formal or informal, express or implied) to dispose of, or to exercise control over the disposal of, the shares` IS FALSE
    `property held in trust consists of or includes the shares and the person has an interest under the trust` IS FALSE
    `the person knows, or has reasonable grounds for believing, that the person has that interest under the trust` IS FALSE
    `the person has entered into a contract to purchase a share` IS TRUE
    `the person has a right, otherwise than by reason of having an interest under a trust, to have a share transferred to the person or to the person's order` IS FALSE
    `the person has the right to acquire a share, or an interest in a share, under an option` IS FALSE
    `the person is entitled, otherwise than as a proxy or representative at a meeting, to exercise or control the exercise of a right attached to a share of which the person is not the registered holder` IS FALSE
    `the thing is a unit in a collective investment scheme that has been subscribed or purchased on an offer of units, or is issued for such an offer and held by the scheme's manager` IS TRUE
    `the person holds the share as bare trustee` IS FALSE
    `the person's ordinary business includes the lending of money` IS FALSE
    `the person holds the interest only by way of security for a transaction entered into in the ordinary course of business in connection with the lending of money` IS FALSE
    `the person holds the interest by reason of holding a prescribed office` IS FALSE
    `the interest is a company's interest in its own shares purchased or otherwise acquired in accordance with sections 76B to 76G (including treasury shares)` IS FALSE
    `the interest is a prescribed interest of a prescribed person or class of persons` IS FALSE
    `the bodies corporate through which the person may be deemed to have the interest` IS EMPTY

§ `s 164(1) and (1A): what the register must show`

-- (1)(a) to (d): each kind of holding the director has, the company must show.
#ASSERT `s 164(1) the company must show the particulars of the holding in its register of the director's shareholdings` `s 164(1)(a) shares in the company or in a related corporation` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 164(1) the company must show the particulars of the holding in its register of the director's shareholdings` `s 164(1)(b) debentures of, or participatory interests made available by, the company or a related corporation` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 164(1) the company must show the particulars of the holding in its register of the director's shareholdings` `s 164(1)(c) rights or options in respect of the acquisition or disposal of shares in the company or a related corporation` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 164(1) the company must show the particulars of the holding in its register of the director's shareholdings` `s 164(1)(d) contracts under which a person has a right to call for or to make delivery of shares in the company or a related corporation` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (2): shares in a wholly-owned subsidiary need not be shown. A flat negative: JUST FALSE.
#ASSERT `s 164(1) the company must show the particulars of the holding in its register of the director's shareholdings` `s 164(1)(a) shares in the company or in a related corporation` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (2) speaks of shares only: a debenture of a wholly-owned subsidiary is still to be shown.
#ASSERT `s 164(1) the company must show the particulars of the holding in its register of the director's shareholdings` `s 164(1)(b) debentures of, or participatory interests made available by, the company or a related corporation` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A holding the director has nothing to do with: the paragraph is limited to holdings of which the director is the holder or in which he or she has an interest. NOTHING.
#ASSERT `s 164(1) the company must show the particulars of the holding in its register of the director's shareholdings` `s 164(1)(a) shares in the company or in a related corporation` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 164(1) the company must show the particulars of the holding in its register of the director's shareholdings` `s 164(1)(c) rights or options in respect of the acquisition or disposal of shares in the company or a related corporation` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A kind of holding that is not one of the four: the list has no "only". NOTHING.
#ASSERT `s 164(1) the company must show the particulars of the holding in its register of the director's shareholdings` `s 164(1) some other holding` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `s 164(1A) the company must show the particulars of the holding in its register of the chief executive officer's shareholdings` `s 164(1A)(a) shares in the company` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 164(1A) the company must show the particulars of the holding in its register of the chief executive officer's shareholdings` `s 164(1A)(b) debentures of the company` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 164(1A) the company must show the particulars of the holding in its register of the chief executive officer's shareholdings` `s 164(1A)(c) rights or options in respect of the acquisition or disposal of shares in the company` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 164(1A) the company must show the particulars of the holding in its register of the chief executive officer's shareholdings` `s 164(1A)(d) contracts under which a person has a right to call for or to make delivery of shares in the company` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 164(1A) the company must show the particulars of the holding in its register of the chief executive officer's shareholdings` `s 164(1A)(a) shares in the company` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 164(1A) the company must show the particulars of the holding in its register of the chief executive officer's shareholdings` `s 164(1A) some other holding` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- The duty to keep the register has no period: nothing to fall due, so no breach path. Done: FULFILLED. Nothing done: RESIDUAL.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 164(1) the company must keep a register showing the particulars for each director` "Acme Pte Ltd" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company "Acme Pte Ltd" DOES `s 164(1) keep the register of the director's shareholdings` AT 1

-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 164(1) the company must keep a register showing the particulars for each director` "Acme Pte Ltd" AT 0 WITH

§ `s 164(3) and (4): the wholly-owned subsidiary`

-- (3): all three conditions: deemed to have complied. A failed "if": JUST FALSE.
#ASSERT `s 164(3) the wholly-owned subsidiary is deemed to have complied with the section for the person` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 164(3) the wholly-owned subsidiary is deemed to have complied with the section for the person` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 164(3) the wholly-owned subsidiary is deemed to have complied with the section for the person` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 164(3) the wholly-owned subsidiary is deemed to have complied with the section for the person` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- (4): the same words as s 5B, so the keel's answer. Members: the other company itself, and a nominee of it: wholly-owned.
#ASSERT `s 164(4) the company is a wholly-owned subsidiary of the other company` (LIST (`s 5B member` OF `s 5B the other corporation`, EMPTY), (`s 5B member` OF `s 5B a nominee of the other corporation`, EMPTY)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (4): one member is a stranger: not wholly-owned (a closed list, "none ... other than").
#ASSERT `s 164(4) the company is a wholly-owned subsidiary of the other company` (LIST (`s 5B member` OF `s 5B the other corporation`, EMPTY), (`s 5B member` OF `s 5B any other person`, EMPTY)) EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `s 164(5) and (6): entering the particulars within 3 days`

-- (5)(b): the date to enter. A transaction: the agreement or, if later, the completion.
#ASSERT `s 164(5)(b) the date the company must enter` TRUE (Date 10 1 2026) (Date 20 1 2026) (Date 5 1 2026) EQUALS Date 20 1 2026
#ASSERT `s 164(5)(b) the date the company must enter` TRUE (Date 20 1 2026) (Date 10 1 2026) (Date 5 1 2026) EQUALS Date 20 1 2026
-- No transaction: the date of the event.
#ASSERT `s 164(5)(b) the date the company must enter` FALSE (Date 10 1 2026) (Date 20 1 2026) (Date 5 1 2026) EQUALS Date 5 1 2026

-- (5)(a): the consideration is entered for holdings acquired after the person became a director or chief executive officer, and "(if any)".
#ASSERT `s 164(5)(a) the company must enter the price or other consideration` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 164(5)(a) the company must enter the price or other consideration` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 164(5)(a) the company must enter the price or other consideration` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- (5): the entry includes the number and description of what the notice relates to.
#ASSERT `s 164(5) the entry in the register includes what the subsection requires it to include` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 164(5) the entry in the register includes what the subsection requires it to include` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- (5): received on 1 March 2026; 3 days after is 4 March (P1: the day of receipt is not counted). In time up to and including the last day; an entry on the day of receipt is not late.
#ASSERT `s 164(5) the company entered the particulars within 3 days after receiving the notice` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 4 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 164(5) the company entered the particulars within 3 days after receiving the notice` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 164(5) the company entered the particulars within 3 days after receiving the notice` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 5 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 164(6) the company entered the particulars of the change within 3 days after receiving the notice` (Date 31 3 2026) (Date 3 4 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 164(6) the company entered the particulars of the change within 3 days after receiving the notice` (Date 31 3 2026) (Date 4 4 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- The rule with its period: the act in 3 days: FULFILLED. In 4 days: BREACH. Nothing yet: RESIDUAL.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 164(5) the company must enter the particulars in its register within 3 days after receiving the notice` "Acme Pte Ltd" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company "Acme Pte Ltd" DOES `s 164(5) enter the particulars in the register` AT 3

-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 164(5) the company must enter the particulars in its register within 3 days after receiving the notice` "Acme Pte Ltd" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company "Acme Pte Ltd" DOES `s 164(5) enter the particulars in the register` AT 4

-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 164(5) the company must enter the particulars in its register within 3 days after receiving the notice` "Acme Pte Ltd" AT 0 WITH

-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 164(6) the company must enter the particulars of the change in its register within 3 days after receiving the notice` "Acme Pte Ltd" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company "Acme Pte Ltd" DOES `s 164(6) enter the particulars of the change in the register` AT 2

-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 164(6) the company must enter the particulars of the change in its register within 3 days after receiving the notice` "Acme Pte Ltd" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company "Acme Pte Ltd" DOES `s 164(6) enter the particulars of the change in the register` AT 5

§ `s 164(7): no notice by reason of the register`

#ASSERT `s 164(7) the company is taken to have notice of, or to be put upon inquiry as to, the right of a person or a share` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 164(7) the company is taken to have notice of, or to be put upon inquiry as to, the right of a person or a share` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 164(8): the register at the registered office, and the charge for inspection`

#ASSERT `s 164(8) the company has kept its register at its registered office` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 164(8) the company has kept its register at its registered office` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A member inspects without charge; any other person pays up to $3.
#ASSERT `s 164(8) the most the company may charge the person for each inspection of the register, in Singapore dollars` TRUE EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 164(8) the most the company may charge the person for each inspection of the register, in Singapore dollars` FALSE EQUALS 3

-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 164(8) the company must keep its register open for inspection` "Acme Pte Ltd" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company "Acme Pte Ltd" DOES `s 164(8) open the register for inspection` AT 1

-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 164(8) the company must keep its register open for inspection` "Acme Pte Ltd" AT 0 WITH

§ `s 164(9): a copy of the register`

-- $1 for every page or part: counting a part page as a page, 5 pages is $5 at most.
#ASSERT `s 164(9) the most the company may charge in advance for the copy, in Singapore dollars` 5 EQUALS 5
-- 21 days, or the longer period the Registrar thinks fit; where the Registrar has allowed none (0), or less than 21, it is 21.
#ASSERT `s 164(9) the number of days the company has to send the copy` 0 EQUALS 21
#ASSERT `s 164(9) the number of days the company has to send the copy` 10 EQUALS 21
#ASSERT `s 164(9) the number of days the company has to send the copy` 30 EQUALS 30
-- The duty arises on a request made on payment in advance; without them the text is silent.
#ASSERT `s 164(9) the company must send the copy to the person` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 164(9) the company must send the copy to the person` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 164(9) the company must send the copy to the person` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Request received on 1 April 2026: 21 days after is 22 April.
#ASSERT `s 164(9) the company sent the copy in time` (Date 1 4 2026) 21 (Date 22 4 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 164(9) the company sent the copy in time` (Date 1 4 2026) 21 (Date 23 4 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 164(9) the company sent the copy in time` (Date 1 4 2026) 30 (Date 1 5 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 164(9) the company must send the copy within the days allowed after the request is received` "Acme Pte Ltd" 21 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company "Acme Pte Ltd" DOES `s 164(9) send the copy of the register to the person` AT 21

-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 164(9) the company must send the copy within the days allowed after the request is received` "Acme Pte Ltd" 21 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company "Acme Pte Ltd" DOES `s 164(9) send the copy of the register to the person` AT 22

-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 164(9) the company must send the copy within the days allowed after the request is received` "Acme Pte Ltd" 21 AT 0 WITH

§ `s 164(10) and (11): the Registrar's notice, and the annual general meeting`

#ASSERT `s 164(10) the company must send the Registrar a copy of its register` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 164(10) the company must send the Registrar a copy of its register` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Notice received 1 May 2026 specifying 14 days: the last day is 15 May.
#ASSERT `s 164(10) the company sent the copy to the Registrar within the time the notice specifies` (Date 1 5 2026) 14 (Date 15 5 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 164(10) the company sent the copy to the Registrar within the time the notice specifies` (Date 1 5 2026) 14 (Date 16 5 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 164(10) the company must send the Registrar a copy of its register within the time the notice specifies` "Acme Pte Ltd" 14 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company "Acme Pte Ltd" DOES `s 164(10) send the Registrar a copy of the register` AT 14

-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 164(10) the company must send the Registrar a copy of its register within the time the notice specifies` "Acme Pte Ltd" 14 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company "Acme Pte Ltd" DOES `s 164(10) send the Registrar a copy of the register` AT 15

-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 164(10) the company must send the Registrar a copy of its register within the time the notice specifies` "Acme Pte Ltd" 14 AT 0 WITH

#ASSERT `s 164(11) the company has complied with the duty to produce its register at each annual general meeting` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 164(11) the company has complied with the duty to produce its register at each annual general meeting` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 164(11) the company has complied with the duty to produce its register at each annual general meeting` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 164(11) the company must produce its register at the commencement of each annual general meeting` "Acme Pte Ltd" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company "Acme Pte Ltd" DOES `s 164(11) produce the register at the commencement of the annual general meeting` AT 1

-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 164(11) the company must produce its register at the commencement of each annual general meeting` "Acme Pte Ltd" AT 0 WITH

§ `s 164(12): the defence`

-- "It is a defence to a prosecution for failing to comply with subsection (1), (1A) or (5) ... if the defendant proves that the failure was due to the failure of the director or chief executive officer to comply with section 165 ...": proved, in the three named failures: a defence; not proved: no defence on these facts (JUST FALSE); a prosecution for another failure (for example subsection (6)): the text does not say (NOTHING).
#ASSERT `s 164(12) the section gives the defendant a defence on these facts` `s 164(12) a failure to comply with subsection (1)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 164(12) the section gives the defendant a defence on these facts` `s 164(12) a failure to comply with subsection (1A)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 164(12) the section gives the defendant a defence on these facts` `s 164(12) a failure to comply with subsection (5)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 164(12) the section gives the defendant a defence on these facts` `s 164(12) a failure to comply with subsection (1)` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 164(12) the section gives the defendant a defence on these facts` `s 164(12) a failure to comply with subsection (5)` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 164(12) the section gives the defendant a defence on these facts` `s 164(12) another failure` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 164(12) the section gives the defendant a defence on these facts` `s 164(12) another failure` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 164(13) to (16): terms, interests and deemed holdings`

#ASSERT `s 164(13)(a) the thing is a participatory interest` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 164(13)(a) the thing is a participatory interest` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 164(13)(b) the person is a person who holds or acquires shares, debentures or participatory interests or an interest in them` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 164(13)(b) the person is a person who holds or acquires shares, debentures or participatory interests or an interest in them` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- (1)(a): the share case is s 7 with the purpose s 164. No interest facts: no interest. A contract to purchase: an interest (s 7(6)(a)).
#ASSERT `s 164(1)(a) the director has an interest in the shares` `s 164 test facts: no interest at all` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 164(1)(a) the director has an interest in the shares` `s 164 test facts: a contract to purchase a share` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A unit that falls under s 7(3) is no interest in a share, so there the answer is no; (14) leaves out s 7(3), so for a debenture or participatory interest the same facts give an interest.
#ASSERT `s 164(1)(a) the director has an interest in the shares` `s 164 test facts: a unit and a contract to purchase` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 164(14) the person has an interest in the debenture or participatory interest` `s 164 test facts: a unit and a contract to purchase` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 164(14) the person has an interest in the debenture or participatory interest` `s 164 test facts: a contract to purchase a share` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 164(14) the person has an interest in the debenture or participatory interest` `s 164 test facts: no interest at all` EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- (15)(a): a wife or husband, or a child under 18, who holds shares or debentures, when not themself a director or chief executive officer.
#ASSERT `s 164(15)(a) the director or chief executive officer is deemed to hold or have an interest or a right in or over the shares or debentures` `s 164(15) the wife or husband` 40 TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 164(15)(a) the director or chief executive officer is deemed to hold or have an interest or a right in or over the shares or debentures` `s 164(15) a child` 17 TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A child of exactly 18 is not "of less than 18 years of age".
#ASSERT `s 164(15)(a) the director or chief executive officer is deemed to hold or have an interest or a right in or over the shares or debentures` `s 164(15) a child` 18 TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 164(15)(a) the director or chief executive officer is deemed to hold or have an interest or a right in or over the shares or debentures` `s 164(15) another person` 40 TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The wife, husband or child is themself a director or chief executive officer: not within the deeming.
#ASSERT `s 164(15)(a) the director or chief executive officer is deemed to hold or have an interest or a right in or over the shares or debentures` `s 164(15) the wife or husband` 40 FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The wife or husband holds nothing.
#ASSERT `s 164(15)(a) the director or chief executive officer is deemed to hold or have an interest or a right in or over the shares or debentures` `s 164(15) the wife or husband` 40 TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

#ASSERT `s 164(15)(b) the contract, assignment, right of subscription or grant is deemed to have been entered into, exercised or made by, or made to, the director or chief executive officer` `s 164(15) the wife or husband` 40 TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 164(15)(b) the contract, assignment, right of subscription or grant is deemed to have been entered into, exercised or made by, or made to, the director or chief executive officer` `s 164(15) a child` 5 TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 164(15)(b) the contract, assignment, right of subscription or grant is deemed to have been entered into, exercised or made by, or made to, the director or chief executive officer` `s 164(15) a child` 18 TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 164(15)(b) the contract, assignment, right of subscription or grant is deemed to have been entered into, exercised or made by, or made to, the director or chief executive officer` `s 164(15) the wife or husband` 40 FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- (16): "child" includes stepson, adopted son, stepdaughter and adopted daughter: the list of inclusions is not closed.
#ASSERT `s 164(16) the person is within the word child` `s 164(16) a son or daughter` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 164(16) the person is within the word child` `s 164(16) a stepson` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 164(16) the person is within the word child` `s 164(16) an adopted son` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 164(16) the person is within the word child` `s 164(16) a stepdaughter` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 164(16) the person is within the word child` `s 164(16) an adopted daughter` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 164(16) the person is within the word child` `s 164(16) another relative` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 164(17): the offence`

-- Default made: the company and every officer in default are guilty. No default: JUST FALSE. A person not named: NOTHING.
#ASSERT `s 164(17) the person is guilty of the offence` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 164(17) the person is guilty of the offence` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 164(17) the person is guilty of the offence` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 164(17) the person is guilty of the offence` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The penalty: a fine up to $15,000 or imprisonment up to 3 years, and $1,000 for each day the offence continues after conviction.
#ASSERT `s 164(17) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST (`s 164(17) penalty` OF 15000, 3, 1000)
#ASSERT `s 164(17) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST (`s 164(17) penalty` OF 15000, 3, 1000)
#ASSERT `s 164(17) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 164(17) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 164(17) the further fine for the days the offence continues after conviction, in Singapore dollars` 0 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 164(17) the further fine for the days the offence continues after conviction, in Singapore dollars` 3 EQUALS 3000
